{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fea6358a-6e7e-4f4f-a318-b9cd9e520167","agentId":"ae7876d470c147f2a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"You are the QA engineer for WP Rocket. Your task is to manually verify the fix for issue #8300 using Playwright against the local WordPress environment at http://localhost:8888.\n\n## What was fixed\n\n**Issue**: The `action_scheduler_run_queue_rucss` cron event continued firing every minute even when the RUCSS (Remove Unused CSS) option was disabled. Root cause: `initialize_rucss_queue_runner()` in `inc/Engine/Common/JobManager/Cron/Subscriber.php` was checking `JobProcessor::is_allowed()`, which returns `true` if ANY factory (including Rocket Insights) is active — instead of checking specifically whether the RUCSS factory is allowed.\n\n**Fix applied**: Changed the guard in `initialize_rucss_queue_runner()` to check `$this->factories['rucss']->manager()->is_allowed()` directly, and added cleanup logic to clear the `action_scheduler_run_queue_rucss` scheduled hook when RUCSS is disabled.\n\n## What to test\n\nYou need to verify two scenarios:\n\n**Scenario A — RUCSS disabled: cron should NOT exist**\n1. Log into WP admin at http://localhost:8888/wp-admin (credentials: admin/password or check if login is needed)\n2. Go to Settings > WP Rocket (or the WP Rocket settings page)\n3. Ensure the \"Remove Unused CSS\" option is DISABLED (unchecked/off)\n4. Save settings if needed\n5. Check cron events — navigate to Tools > Cron Events (requires a plugin like WP Crontrol or WP Control), or check via the URL `http://localhost:8888/wp-admin/tools.php?page=crontrol_admin_manage_page`\n6. Verify that `action_scheduler_run_queue_rucss` does NOT appear in the list of scheduled cron events\n7. Take a screenshot of the cron events list\n\n**Scenario B — RUCSS enabled: cron SHOULD exist**\n1. Go to WP Rocket settings and ENABLE \"Remove Unused CSS\"\n2. Save settings\n3. Trigger the init hook by visiting the site or reloading wp-admin\n4. Check cron events again\n5. Verify that `action_scheduler_run_queue_rucss` IS now scheduled\n6. Take a screenshot\n\n## WP Rocket settings page\nThe WP Rocket settings are accessible at: `http://localhost:8888/wp-admin/options-general.php?page=wprocket`\nThe RUCSS option is in the \"File Optimization\" tab.\n\n## Notes\n- If a cron plugin isn't installed, you can check via WP CLI if available: `wp cron event list --format=table`\n- The WordPress admin login page is at: http://localhost:8888/wp-admin/\n- If you can't access the cron events page via a plugin, try: http://localhost:8888/wp-admin/tools.php?page=crontrol_admin_manage_page\n\nReport: what you tested, what you found, screenshots taken, and whether the fix behaves correctly."},"uuid":"81fbdc1b-f55d-41ed-aaef-6245b32e85ee","timestamp":"2026-05-19T12:16:31.325Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/gaelrobin/Local Sites/bwu/app/public/wp-content/plugins/backwpup-pro","sessionId":"a1b6853a-1b9a-4b8e-8b31-6672b519a1db","version":"2.1.143","gitBranch":"test/nudges","slug":"precious-imagining-cloud"}
